      "attackPlan": "Summit plays A/B Sites. Start rounds on a slow default: spread across mid and both approaches, let Initiators send recon into the site your team leans toward, and keep one flank watcher so you aren't collapsed on from behind. When you commit to an execute, Controllers should smoke the site's key sightlines (see the callouts below for names to communicate with) before the entry Duelist commits -- smoking and entering at the same time gets your entry killed by an angle that was never covered. Initiators clear common off-angle holds with flashes/recon just ahead of the entry, and the rest of the team trades through the doorway rather than stacking behind the entry fragger.",
      "defensePlan": "On defense, split to cover both/all sites with information first: an Initiator or Sentinel utility piece watching mid or the most common flank buys the rest of the team rotation time. Don't hard-peek early utility -- trade off default info instead. If the site falls, fall back to a rotation-friendly angle and regroup as a retake unit rather than feeding one at a time; retakes on Summit want your Controller to re-smoke the plant's sightline and your Initiator to clear common post-plant lurk spots before anyone pushes onto the plant.",
